{number: 122}
{title: A Wonderful Savior}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [D] wonderful Savior is Jesus my Lord,
A [G] wonderful Savior to [D] me;
He hideth my soul in the cleft of the rock,
Where [A7] rivers of pleasure I [D] see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [D] hideth my soul in the cleft of the rock
That [G] shadows a dry, thirsty [D] land;
He hideth my life in the depths of His love,
And [A7] covers me there with His [D] hand,
And [G] covers me [D] there with His [A7] [D] hand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
A [D] wonderful Savior is Jesus my Lord,
He [G] taketh my burden a-[D] way;
He holdeth me up, and I shall not be moved,
He [A7] giveth me strength as my [D] day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
With [D] numberless blessings each moment He crowns,
And, [G] filled with His fullness di-[D] vine,
I sing in my rapture, oh, glory to God
For [A7] such a Redeemer as [D] mine!
{end_of_verse}
